Boot animation through KMS, on the largest panel only

The fbdev console is mirrored to every panel at the size they share (the
Thor's bottom panel, 1080x1240), so on the top panel the splash covered only
part of the screen and could not be centred. --animate now draws through
KMS on the largest connected panel with a buffer of its own size, and turns
the others off; one-shot modes stay on /dev/fb0 (a KMS picture goes away
when the process exits). At boot the panels may still be probing, so it
retries for 5 s before falling back to /dev/fb0, and logs which it used.

